<problem><title>Video review question</title>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>Using the rule outlined in the video, compute the derivative of the following power functions:
  <ol>
    <li><m>f(x) = x^3 \;\;\; f'(x) = </m> <answer name="ans1">3x^2</answer></li>
    <li><m>f(x) = x^7 \;\;\; f'(x) = </m> <answer name="ans2">7x^6</answer></li>
    <li><m>f(x) = x^{-5} \;\;\; f'(x) = </m> <answer name="ans3">-5 x^(-6)</answer></li>
    <li><m>f(x) = x^{3/2} \;\;\; f'(x) = </m> <answer name="ans4" symbolicEquality="true" simplifyOnCompare="true">(3/2)x^(1/2)</answer>
    , where <m>f</m> is restricted to the domain:
      <answer inline="true">
        <choice credit="1"><m>x > 0</m></choice>
        <choice><m>x &lt; 0</m></choice>
        <choice><m>x \neq 0</m></choice>
      </answer>
    </li>
  </ol>
</p>
<feedback condition="$ans1.numSubmissions = 1  and $ans1.creditAchieved != 1"> See <ref to="$vid_section">Key Moment 1</ref> in the video for some worked examples like this.</feedback>
<feedback condition="$ans2.numSubmissions = 1  and $ans2.creditAchieved != 1">See <ref to="$vid_section">Key Moment 1</ref> in the video for some worked examples like this.</feedback>
<feedback condition="$ans3.numSubmissions = 1  and $ans3.creditAchieved != 1">See <ref to="$vid_section">Key Moment 2</ref> in the video for some worked examples like this.</feedback>
<feedback condition="$ans4.numSubmissions = 1  and $ans4.creditAchieved != 1">See <ref to="$vid_section">Key Moment 2</ref> in the video for some worked examples like this.</feedback>

<feedback condition="$ans1.numSubmissions > 1  and $ans1.creditAchieved != 1">To apply the power rule
  <me>f'(x) = n x^{n-1}\;\;\; \text{where} \;\;\;f(x) = x^n</me> 
  we first multiply the entire function by the value of the exponent of <m>f</m>, which is <m>n</m>. Then, we subtract <m>1</m> from the exponent of <m>f</m> to obtain the value of the exponent for <m>f'(x)</m>:
  <md>
    <mrow>f'(x)\amp, \;\;\; \text{where} \;\;\;f(x) = x^3</mrow>
    <mrow>f'(x)\amp = 3\cdot x^{3 - 1}</mrow>
    <mrow>f'(x)\amp = 3x^2</mrow>
  </md>
</feedback>
<feedback condition="$ans2.numSubmissions > 1  and $ans2.creditAchieved != 1">To apply the power rule
  <me>f'(x) = n x^{n-1}\;\;\; \text{where} \;\;\;f(x) = x^n</me> 
  we first multiply the entire function by the value of the exponent of <m>f</m>, which is <m>n</m>. Then, we subtract <m>1</m> from the exponent of <m>f</m> to obtain the value of the exponent for <m>f'(x)</m>:
  <md>
    <mrow>f'(x)\amp, \;\;\; \text{where} \;\;\;f(x) = x^7</mrow>
    <mrow>f'(x)\amp = 7\cdot x^{7 - 1}</mrow>
    <mrow>f'(x)\amp = 7x^6</mrow>
  </md>
</feedback>
<feedback condition="$ans3.numSubmissions > 1  and $ans3.creditAchieved != 1">To apply the power rule
  <me>f'(x) = n x^{n-1}\;\;\; \text{where} \;\;\;f(x) = x^{-5}</me> 
  we first multiply the entire function by the value of the exponent of <m>f</m>, which is <m>n</m>. Then, we subtract <m>1</m> from the exponent of <m>f</m> to obtain the value of the exponent for <m>f'(x)</m>:
  <md>
    <mrow>f'(x)\amp, \;\;\; \text{where} \;\;\;f(x) = x^{-5}</mrow>
    <mrow>f'(x)\amp = -5\cdot x^{-5 - 1}</mrow>
    <mrow>f'(x)\amp = -5x^{-6}\;\;\; \text{or}\;\;\;- \frac{5}{x^6}</mrow>
  </md>
</feedback>
<feedback condition="$ans4.numSubmissions > 1  and $ans4.creditAchieved != 1">To apply the power rule
  <me>f'(x) = n x^{n-1}\;\;\; \text{where} \;\;\;f(x) = x^n</me> 
  we first multiply the entire function by the value of the exponent of <m>f</m>, which is <m>n</m>. Then, we subtract <m>1</m> from the exponent of <m>f</m> to obtain the value of the exponent for <m>f'(x)</m>:
  <md>
    <mrow>f'(x)\amp, \;\;\; \text{where} \;\;\;f(x) = x^{\frac{3}{2}}</mrow>
    <mrow>f'(x)\amp = \frac{3}{2}\cdot x^{\frac{3}{2} - 1}</mrow>
    <mrow>f'(x)\amp = \frac{3}{2} x^{\frac{1}{2}}\;\;\; \text{or}\;\;\;\frac{3 \sqrt{x}}{2}</mrow>
  </md>
</feedback>
  
  
  
</exercise>
</problem>